ac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u,\\,y(u,v,w)={v}^{3}+{w}^{3},\\,z(u,v,w)=v+w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =3{v}^{2} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =3{w}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2} & 3{w}^{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}3{v}^{2} & 3{w}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(3{v}^{2}-3{w}^{2}) \\\\  & =3({v}^{2}-{w}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 3({v}^{2}-{w}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ {v}^{2}-{w}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation ${v}^{2}-{w}^{2}=0$ defines a pair of intersecting planes $v=w$ and $v=-w.$" 13194139536164 true] [17592186386825 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386826 13194139536164 true] [17592186386825 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386827 13194139536164 true] [17592186386825 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386828 13194139536164 true] [17592186386825 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386829 13194139536164 true] [17592186386825 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386830 13194139536164 true] [17592186386825 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536164 true] [17592186386825 1041 "selection" 13194139536164 true] [17592186386825 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386828 13194139536164 true] [17592186386825 1110 #uuid "c90c68ec-18c8-5659-b3a4-9cda8f219fc7" 13194139536164 true] [17592186386826 1034 "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." 13194139536164 true] [17592186386826 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536164 true] [17592186386826 1111 #uuid "4c3ca069-e60e-5f1a-8d5e-3ad3541fa855" 13194139536164 true] [17592186386827 1034 "The critical